WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.709
Let's go next to our caller from the five
zero three area code.

00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:05.600
Who's calling today from five zero three

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.220
Hey David, this is Warren from Portland, Oregon.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.070
How are you?

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.309
Hey there.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:14.309
Good.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:18.550
It's so recently Russell and Bob mentioned
that, uh, Trump was, as he referred to him

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.470
as like mr man.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:26.330
And it's, it's become so troubling how so
many people, I mean, mainly the base has seen

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:33.470
masculinity and Trump as this epitome of,
of manhood and that fuels their, their judgements

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:39.079
towards those that aren't as man, like I guess,
um, you know, the snowflake line and all that.

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:41.899
And at the same time though, I'm curious about
your opinion.

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:47.200
There's this movement of, of you know, LGBT
and kind of an awakening of what is masculine

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.200
and feminine.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.660
And I'm wondering like how you see it kind
of coming out in politics cause it's coming

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:58.629
out, I think in media a lot faster, the allowance
of, of such, um, you know, definitions in

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:02.170
definitions of, of masculinity and femininity.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:07.889
But how do you see it, um, coming out, uh,
in the political world, which I don't know

00:01:07.889 --> 00:01:08.889
nearly enough.

00:01:08.889 --> 00:01:13.369
I feel like the way that it's coming out is
extremely stratified.

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:18.069
So what I mean by that is the following, um,
take somebody like Barack Obama.

00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:26.490
Now stereotypes around black men are often
about, uh, you know, hyper masculine hypersexualized

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.419
often in society including in portrayals in
media.

00:01:31.419 --> 00:01:37.460
Often there are, uh, you know, illusions to
the black man as more likely to become violent.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.799
And you know, we've studied all this stuff
academically about portrayal portrayals of

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:42.799
black men.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:52.489
Now at the same time Barack Obama is, um,
uh, of, of very well educated, um, the type

00:01:52.489 --> 00:01:59.359
of person that fits much more into sort of
to use the, uh, the arbitrary dichotomy of

00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:01.419
the fighter versus the lover.

00:02:01.419 --> 00:02:06.200
Barack Obama far more fits into the idea of
the lover, the thinker, whatever.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.489
If you look at, you know, his relationships
with other people, how he interacts with his

00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:11.500
kids and whatever.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:18.251
Where is Donald Trump in many ways is portrayed
and seen by his supporters as kind of the

00:02:18.251 --> 00:02:20.709
epitome of the alpha male.

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:25.540
And I do think that some of these roles are
changing because there's a huge swath of society

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:31.370
where when they see Barack Obama, not a guy
likely to get into the types of, for lack

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:36.780
of a better term, pissing matches that Donald
Trump gets himself in a, into not the type

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:42.569
of guy to make the types of threats that Donald
Trump makes for a huge part of America that

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:48.420
is seen as the adult in charge, in the room,
way to behave where Donald Trump, despite

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:55.180
checking a lot of the stereotypical boxes
of the alpha male threats, loud, boisterous,

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.459
pushing his way around to get to the front
of the picture with the world leaders, insulting

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:06.269
people, all of this stuff, Donald Trump in
reality is very much the snowflake that the

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:09.569
right likes to portray many on the left to
be.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.719
So I think the answer to your question in
a very long winded way is it depends who you

00:03:13.719 --> 00:03:14.719
ask for.

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:20.109
A huge part of the American electorate, those
old standards of alpha versus beta and masculinity

00:03:20.109 --> 00:03:24.290
still persist and a lot of those people are
supporting Donald Trump.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:28.700
There's a whole other world out there because
we have a country that is so divided culturally

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.629
as much as it is politically, um, uh, where
those norms have drastically changed.

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:37.560
And I think that that's a very good thing.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.959
Yeah, it seems like it's an, I, I hate to
stereotype, but seems like the Democrats are

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:46.599
pushing an open mindedness and the Republicans
are holding onto a close minded desk.

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:50.689
Maybe I can call some of the time and ask,
but what if the Republicans here to teach

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:53.749
us, I mean it can't be that one sided or is
it,

00:03:53.749 --> 00:03:57.060
I, I'm not sure I know what you mean.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:02.459
Um, like it seems like we, I feel as a Democrat,
I am part of a group of people who are, who

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:04.480
are evolving, um, to a place.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.519
Uh, we're, we're teaching the Republicans
about compassion and what real manhood is.

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:11.639
Power is not insulting.

00:04:11.639 --> 00:04:12.639
It's compassionate.

00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:16.030
It looks maybe snowflakey but it's actually
strength.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.650
Yes, absolutely.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.650
And I don't know that they're getting it.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.750
I think some of them may be, are

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.590
what I'm wondering is, is it that one sided
in a good way?

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:28.750
I think where we are here to kind of help
others get it,

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.520
but that sounds a little self righteous.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.770
It's not totally one sided.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.450
It's not totally one sided.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:40.780
But at the national level, at the national
level, I think that it is very one sided in

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.380
terms of the messages we get in media.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:48.240
I think in practice there are plenty of people
who are, you know, for low taxes who also

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:54.930
are just as empathetic and comfortable with
sort of more modern, uh, um, understandings

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:59.680
of masculinity than, uh, than what we see
represented by Republicans at the national

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.680
level.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.699
Very important topic and I hope to talk about
it again.

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:04.170
Really appreciate the phone call.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.740
A very, very nice to hear from you.

